From 8e29651b21ad1e112a3b1e733d9726f51591b11d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jesus David Saavedra Latorre <iam.jesusd88@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 21:42:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 04/35] feat(digitizer): add pinch to zoom in mouse fallback

With DIGITIZER_MOUSE_PINCH_ENABLE, two finger gestures scroll with the
finger midpoint. When the finger distance change passes
DIGITIZER_PINCH_THRESHOLD and exceeds the midpoint movement, the gesture
becomes a pinch: the modifiers from the weak digitizer_pinch_mods_user()
are held as weak mods and the distance change is sent as vertical
scroll. The modifiers are released on every exit from the two finger
gesture.

The mac keymap enables it and adds PINCH_MOD_CYCLE to cycle Cmd, Ctrl
and plain scroll, stored in the user EEPROM block, plus a readme.
